<Solution>

  <!--
    The reference graph, and it is the whole reason this template exists. docs/plan/27 § The three
    assemblies a game writes: getting this wrong on day one is the kind of mistake that is
    discovered in month six.

      Contracts  ← everybody. The wire, and the shard vocabulary. No Orleans, no engine.
      Shared     ← client + realm. The rules both ends run, once.
      Realm      → Shared, Contracts, Vixen.Live.Realm
      Client     → Shared, Contracts, Vixen.App — and nothing from the control plane (ADR-017)
      Content    → nobody. Addresses, which both ends resolve out of a catalog they agree on.
  -->
  <Project Path="VixenMmo1.Contracts/VixenMmo1.Contracts.csproj" />
  <Project Path="VixenMmo1.Shared/VixenMmo1.Shared.csproj" />
  <Project Path="VixenMmo1.Realm/VixenMmo1.Realm.csproj" />
  <Project Path="VixenMmo1.Client/VixenMmo1.Client.csproj" />

</Solution>
